ts":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:04:55-07:00","id":634985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=634947#post634947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, considering the playable sects on revised cire books. We could separate which case and decide which one would win in each case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but then the Technocracy, the Crafts and the Changing Breeds of the Werewolf gameline are also viable options. All of them are valid player characters and troupes since Revised, and in the case of the Changing Breeds, way before that. I'm not sure what the differentiating distrinction is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:20:16-07:00","id":635024,"title":"","content":"Oh, nevermind. You want to do Revised Core book splat pages. Then yes, Traditions vs. Garou vs Camarilla/Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T05:49:20-07:00","id":635700,"title":"","content":"(A) mages. Because they can hide from the other splats (at least a good portion of them) and thus take their time to seek out the others hiding places and then just destroy them through magic.<br /> <br /> (B) mages. Because Voormas would look up annoyed, pay a visit to Senex on Charon, together with whatever other Entropy Archmasters are around and do an Entropy 7 ritual that would destine vampires and werewolves to loose the fight. Who cares about the details, time to go back to their (respective) work, if they don't kill each other while in such close umbral proximity.<br /> <br /> Also the higher ups of the TU would launch a device into the sun that causes the sun to emit a new near infra red wavelength that pierces all materials, thus burning all vampires around the world. Also they would release small amounts of highly active silver particles into the air around earth, transported by shiftersensitive carrier agents, eliminating all werewolves in a matter of weeks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T07:09:50-07:00","id":635751,"title":"","content":"Of the splats Mages, because whatever can't actually be dealt with a Master of Time could imprison for eternity.<br /> <br /> When all things WW are considered there are only a few things I can think of that could escape an Archmage / Oracle of Time. <br /> <br /> Wrinkle. Im not sure he can be imprisoned but he can surely imprison them. <br /> <br /> Gabriel. He stands in the presence of God, enough said.<br /> <br /> Lucifer for similar reasons but I kind of think him to be beyond the scope of this as to include him one could argue to include God as well.<br /> <br /> And lastly Grandmother (The Grand Maw). I don't think you can defeat / imprison the embodiment of thermal dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T07:53:59-07:00","id":635806,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are by far the strongest sort of player character. At least in terms of what player characters do - fight, sneak into or out of places, get surprised, have to deal with proactive enemies, etc. Despite that, vampires and mages tend to have abilities which lend themselves better to a protracted conflict. Vampires can mass produce legions of human or ghoul servants, so if there is a full scale war between werewolves and vampires, werewolves would find themselves in a war with humanity too. Vampires can also replenish their numbers rapidly and can have the lowest generation vampires do all of the embracing - since they're completely unified.<br /> <br /> That said, mages will win this most likely. Mages' extreme versatility, their unification, their ability to win with greater planning. These all point to them being able to crush the other sides unless we go with Antediluvians as plot devices. Mages could just scan the world for other types of creatures and then teleport bombs into every elder's haven or werewolf Cairn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:33:48-07:00","id":636100,"title":"","content":"Ok, I see that mages are winning. So I want you to consider this.<br /> <br /> In (A) I believe that Mages indeed would win, altough such a large ritual (the only way they can win) extremily vulgar could have paradox consequences.<br /> <br /> In (B) we have all antediluvians and caine himself. I don't think simply throwing sun rays on them would be enough, since porbably all of them could have/develop fortitute 10 in seconds. Also, consider that they are political and manipulation masters taht could multiply their numbers almost instantly AND blood bond mages (what happens when this happen?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:45:55-07:00","id":636121,"title":"","content":"Cain can be dealt with without much hassle by those I mentioned previously, and Antedeluvians are much easier than he. Even if combined.<br /> <br /> Why worry about Fortutude when I can teleport them to the sun. Yes they do/can have resistance but building the effect in an umbral realm for how ever long is needed will overpower that easy enough. Yes archmages are that rediculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Spelling 08-22-2015, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:17:31-07:00","id":636301,"title":"","content":"Mages would win simply because you threw up everything that holds them, except paradox. And them made them don't give a fuck to Paradox, if it means to get rid of competition.<br /> <br /> If you put restrictions on the scenario, other than Earth and Humanity be still existing afterwards, them you can level thing up a bit. To hold Mages from simply winning, you have to either make them have a reason to avoid Paradox or strip them from the time to do the most awesome things.<br /> <br /> And, of course, them you simply doom the Mages to extinction, because you stripped them from what makes them a force to be feared. In that case, I'll go with Vampires. In both scenarios. The Fera will put a long and gruesome fight, and learn quickly how to adapt to a vampire-style of war, but they simply don't have all the resources, numbers and influence over society (even Shadow Lords and Glass Walker coming close to this) to actually hold against all of Vampire society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:19:29-07:00","id":636303,"title":"","content":"They would destroy each other and Changelings would inherit the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:24:56-07:00","id":636314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=636303#post636303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would destroy each other and Changelings would inherit the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long live the Fae!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T16:43:19-07:00","id":636429,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar enough with the mage scenario. Archmages are mages with high arete/spheres?<br /> They can do anything in umbra? And oracle of time?<br /> <br /> As for caine, he could just create disciplines or use path of mercury znd teleport back to earth. I don't think he can be taken doen easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T16:51:09-07:00","id":636434,"title":"","content":"The umbra possibly removes alot of restrictions for paradox. Archmages use spheres over 5 that were printed a looong time ago. Probably behind the back of the creator of the game..<br /> <br /> Oracles are basically people who say : let's wait a little bit, i do not need to ascend. There antidiluvian equivalent. Cain is ascended equivalent.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why white wolf got rid of most of the archmages in their settings <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","user":"AgentCunningham","date":". 08-22-2015, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T17:13:11-07:00","id":636472,"title":"","content":"Well, if you include the very most powerful beings in each faction, then you essentially have gods with undefined amounts of power against gods with undefined amounts of power. There isn't really a way to answer that question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T19:30:05-07:00","id":636543,"title":"","content":"Very true, those are my exact feelings<br /> <br /> Now, just for fun...<br /> Forces 9 can create new Fundamental Forces, like Gravity, or Electromagnetism.<br /> So, as a theory, an insanely powerful Archmaster could use Forces 9/Life 5-7/Matter 5-7 to create the FuckCaine Force, a pervasive camp that surrounds the universe, which has the effect of &quot;naturally&quot; transforming vitae into sunlight. Would that work?, It's so insane as it sounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-22-2015, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T19:59:15-07:00","id":636577,"title":"","content":"So not to criticize, but isn't discussing archmages vs Ante's, 2nd gen and Caine 100% pointless since all of their powers are more or less undefined?<br /> <br /> And since they're being counted out entirely, shouldn't the Garou's allies in the core book count? That would bring in all sorts of Incarna and Celestines. And yes, I realize mages have allies in the spirit worlds as well, but I would certainly argue that they have less than the Garou in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T20:15:20-07:00","id":636588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=636577#post636577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not to criticize, but isn't discussing archmages vs Ante's, 2nd gen and Caine 100% pointless since all of their powers are more or less undefined?<br /> <br /> And since they're being counted out entirely, shouldn't the Garou's allies in the core book count? That would bring in all sorts of Incarna and Celestines. And yes, I realize mages have allies in the spirit worlds as well, but I would certainly argue that they have less than the Garou in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the most powerful being that is an actual Garou, not just a spirit ally? I am thinking that this is Number Two, who is a Black Spiral Dancer but I guess would be on the Garou side in this scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T20:32:35-07:00","id":636592,"title":"","content":"Number Two or Hakaken (now a Wyrm Totem). Nightmaster is high powered in concept, being fundamentally connected to the Abyss (Garou Abyss, arguably not the Lasombra Abyss). There should actually be a whole isle of Rank 6 Fianna. Rites to summon Incarna are perfectly doable. There are a few gifts to do so instantly. Totem Form boosts power tremendously.<br /> <br /> Mostly just throwing ideas out there since the Garou aren't even being considered. Summoning literal Gods comes a lot easier to Garou than to Mages. Just because a lot of Garou enemies don't have &quot;Plot Device&quot; in their stat block doesn't mean the Garou should be counted out. None of those &quot;Plot Device&quot; antagonists are actually supposed to be fought in Vampire or Mage either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T20:55:55-07:00","id":636595,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Werewolf: the Apocalypse has crazy high powered stuff just like the other game lines. I guess that mages are more associated with their high powered elements because there is a more gradual continuum between mage player characters and the archmages or oracles than there is between werewolf player characters and the godlike beings of the werewolf lines. <br /> <br /> With every faction's plot device beings fighting each other, there is no way to say who would win, but it seems like they could essentially destroy humanity, and all of the player character level beings, and maybe even the planet itself as collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T04:12:56-07:00","id":636872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=636100#post636100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In (B) we have all antediluvians and caine himself. I don't think simply throwing sun rays on them would be enough, since porbably all of them could have/develop fortitute 10 in seconds. Also, consider that they are political and manipulation masters taht could multiply their numbers almost instantly AND blood bond mages (what happens when this happen?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The sun was enough to kill the Ravnos Antedelluvian, and he's one of the guys who invented Fortitude.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T04:17:58-07:00","id":636873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=636595#post636595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Werewolf: the Apocalypse has crazy high powered stuff just like the other game lines. I guess that mages are more associated with their high powered elements because there is a more gradual continuum between mage player characters and the archmages or oracles than there is between werewolf player characters and the godlike beings of the werewolf lines.<br /> <br /> With every faction's plot device beings fighting each other, there is no way to say who would win, but it seems like they could essentially destroy humanity, and all of the player character level beings, and maybe even the planet itself as collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What really bugs me, though is how in heaven's blazes do you imagine them making a unified front. Camarilla and Sabbat? Antedeluvians working together? Nephandi and anyone? Black Spirals and anyone? The whole exercise is so random that I don't get what the point is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T05:03:38-07:00","id":636891,"title":"","content":"I think people are overlooking Caine's most powerful asset: God cursed him so that anyone who tries to hurt him (or does hurt him, depending on the interpretation) gets back what they give seven times. The only person who could hurt Caine (other than God) was Lilith, because she is effectively God's equal/other half. Everyone else would be obliterated before they could destroy him or shortly afterwards.<br /> <br /> Lilith, being a proto-mage, would likely destroy everyone in the world and be the sole survivor. She has no particular loyalty to mages or vampires, because she's a different order of being now. She might save her own 'children', though, depending on which aspect of her personality is ascendant at the time.<br /> <br /> I imagine she'd then go for her revenge on Yahweh. That might be a stalemate (in Revelations of the Dark Mother, it's indicated both he and she are mere manifestations of a greater, non-personified Godhead, which has a range of avatars known as The Shining Ones).<br /> <br /> If the Neverborn are indeed dead Primordials (beings who existed before the gods/celestines), they might be earlier manifestations of the Godhead which might stand with their still-living counterparts in Malfeas (or outside the universe, depending on what you believe) to defeat the gods.<br /> <br /> Then there wouldn't be much left for anyone to claim victory, since the Neverborn want the destruction of all reality. Except maybe Grandmother (and she's more a symbol of the Godhead's destructive side, rather than a distinct, conscious entity). The Godhead (perhaps itself a duality of Prime/Oblivion) wins in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:42:20-07:00","id":636933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=636873#post636873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What really bugs me, though is how in heaven's blazes do you imagine them making a unified front. Camarilla and Sabbat? Antedeluvians working together? Nephandi and anyone? Black Spirals and anyone? The whole exercise is so random that I don't get what the point is.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, some of those factions could work together if the circumstances were right. I'd say that they least likely are the Black Spiral Dancers and Gaian Garou. They are so diametrically opposed that it would be hard to imagine anything making them work together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T07:38:46-07:00","id":637003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=636933#post636933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In theory, some of those factions could work together if the circumstances were right. I'd say that they least likely are the Black Spiral Dancers and Gaian Garou. They are so diametrically opposed that it would be hard to imagine anything making them work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of the Apocalypse scenarios, where the Weaver is the end opposition, the Spirals show up to the grand moot to help the Gaian Garou. How it goes from there is up to whoever is playing and running the game, but it is a proposed idea. I always thought it was a rather amusing scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T04:12:05-07:00","id":637870,"title":"","content":"It was actually my favorite scenario in Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Even in case A (just Revised core books allowed, so to speak), things can escalate rather quickly, but it is possible to hold Earth together and keep alive enough of humanity for the OP's purpose with the question. But scenario B is just the end of everything, unless you assume that such beings will hold enough of themselves to not show up, in this case it turns into scenario A again.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't being considered by many because they're rather limited in approaches and, more importantly, in numbers. To think about mystical powers here becomes irrelevant. Sure, they have as many incredible powers as vampires, but that's just it, they kind of cancel out each other in that. What remains is ties to society (and to potential resources) and numbers.<br /> <br /> That, and, well, Mages DO win through mystical power, but because their versatility is impossible to match. They simply need to do the right ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T09:42:53-07:00","id":638113,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with the scenario is that, if kept to their general characters, none of the groups would allow it to get to a battle royale.<br /> <br /> Garou are used to being out-numbered by equal or stronger forces, and thus their tactics should be more guerilla warfare and ambushes than outright battles. They're wolves, after all, hunters and predators, not soldiers.<br /> <br /> Vampires generally have infiltrated human society to a scary extent. They generally know how to manipulate not only their own resources, but that of the humans around them, as well as their underlings. Vampires are ideally the masters of long term planning. A Prince or Elder ought to be buying up land, having woods and libraries cleared away for other useful things, siccing the police and other mortal institutions onto their enemies, sending the lesser vampires out in packs, and so on.<br /> <br /> Mages ought to be using their own resources, their chantries and alliances, gathering information and using carefully executed rituals to steal away or peck away at the Vampires' power bases and the Werewolves's caerns and resources.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think the Mages would probably win, if only because Vampires have fairly severe liabilities once you get them cornered (or if you find their lairs during the day), and Werewolves generally lack the capacity to manipulate the human world and weapons that the other two groups do. But it'd be a long time before they get to the battle royale stage, if ever.<br /> <br /> If somehow they did, I think my money would be on the Garou. Assuming that the Mages did not have time to prepare. If the Mages do have advanced warning, then Mages. But it wouldn't be pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T11:11:54-07:00","id":638205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638113#post638113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem with the scenario is that, if kept to their general characters, none of the groups would allow it to get to a battle royale.<br /> <br /> Garou are used to being out-numbered by equal or stronger forces, and thus their tactics should be more guerilla warfare and ambushes than outright battles. They're wolves, after all, hunters and predators, not soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the fact that they're fighting an asymmetric war is true, nothing else about the statement is. Their predatory nature is subordinated under the need to tear apart other monsters as the shock troops and line infantry of Gaia. Wolf was combined with human and given the mandate to destroy the most obvious threats, which is why they stopped doing so well after they killed many of the Fera and completely disabled much of their support network. As a whole, all of the Changers could be likened to having a military and support role, and unluckily for them, general support and military action en masse doesn't really do much when you absolutely need specialists to accomplish a goal..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T11:47:48-07:00","id":638239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638205#post638205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the fact that they're fighting an asymmetric war is true, nothing else about the statement is. Their predatory nature is subordinated under the need to tear apart other monsters as the shock troops and line infantry of Gaia. Wolf was combined with human and given the mandate to destroy the most obvious threats, which is why they stopped doing so well after they killed many of the Fera and completely disabled much of their support network. As a whole, all of the Changers could be likened to having a military and support role, and unluckily for them, general support and military action en masse doesn't really do much when you absolutely need specialists to accomplish a goal..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the correction. I'm least familiar with Werewolf of all the main lines (or possibly Hunter). I'm not surprised that I managed to get it completely wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T13:24:33-07:00","id":638304,"title":"","content":"How many of each splat there are running around the WoD is really worth looking at as well. At the very least it gives an idea of starting numbers. And I know plenty of people disagree with canon populations and just add more of each supernatural type as necessary to make their chronicles interesting. That being said, what I remember from canon is (and these numbers I seem to remember being from various ST handbooks):<br /> <br /> One of the Garou books placed their total numbers somewhere around 13,000. This shouldn't include Spirals which number about 3 tribes combined so another 3000 more at least. 16,000 total.<br /> Mages are 1 in a million so about 6000 back then, closer to 7000 now (due to human population increasing by a billion).<br /> Vampires are 1 in 100,000. 1/3 of which are kue-jin. So 60,000 total back then (40,000 cainites) and 70,000 now. That means about 46,000 vampires to start.<br /> <br /> So Vampires are way, way ahead in numbers to start off a conflict like this. Not saying this will be a deciding factor but it will certainly help.<br /> <br /> I can look through my books when I get home to cite sources for the numbers, should anyone really deem it necessary. Like I said, they are from memory, so if anyone have references for different numbers for the populations, by all means throw them up.<br /> <br /> Also, at least according to one of the scenarios, just what's in the Revised books should count, and so I don't think Arch-Mages are even considered since I don't think they are covered in the book.<br /> Another thought: if you do include the other Changing Breeds alongside the Garou, the outcome changes a lot I think (as does their numbers). As was stated, the Garou were only ever meant to be soldiers. Having the support Gaia meant for them makes all the difference. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T13:53:52-07:00","id":638324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638304#post638304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Vampires are way, way ahead in numbers to start off a conflict like this. Not saying this will be a deciding factor but it will certainly help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are also the only major splat in the physical world that can quickly and reliably increase their numbers should something like a planetwide genocidal war erupt. I think that would give them a substantial advantage as a &quot;species&quot; in the trenches against werecreatures, mages, and changelings. Of course, I tend to think if such a war ever broke out and revealed the existence of real supernatural creatures to the masses, eventually the wraiths would be the only supernatural creatures left in large numbers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T14:15:17-07:00","id":638339,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, at least according to one of the scenarios, just what's in the Revised books should count, and so I don't think Arch-Mages are even considered since I don't think they are covered in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Masters of the Art</i> it's THE book on Archmages, and it' from (early) Revised. It has post-AvatarStorm data. Not that I think they should be used (albeit option B demands it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, I tend to think if such a war ever broke out and revealed the existence of real supernatural creatures to the masses, eventually the wraiths would be the only supernatural creatures left in large numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>XDXD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-24-2015, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T14:49:36-07:00","id":638367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638304#post638304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of each splat there are running around the WoD is really worth looking at as well. At the very least it gives an idea of starting numbers. And I know plenty of people disagree with canon populations and just add more of each supernatural type as necessary to make their chronicles interesting. That being said, what I remember from canon is (and these numbers I seem to remember being from various ST handbooks):<br /> <br /> One of the Garou books placed their total numbers somewhere around 13,000. This shouldn't include Spirals which number about 3 tribes combined so another 3000 more at least. 16,000 total.<br /> Mages are 1 in a million so about 6000 back then, closer to 7000 now (due to human population increasing by a billion).<br /> Vampires are 1 in 100,000. 1/3 of which are kue-jin. So 60,000 total back then (40,000 cainites) and 70,000 now. That means about 46,000 vampires to start.<br /> <br /> So Vampires are way, way ahead in numbers to start off a conflict like this. Not saying this will be a deciding factor but it will certainly help.<br /> <br /> I can look through my books when I get home to cite sources for the numbers, should anyone really deem it necessary. Like I said, they are from memory, so if anyone have references for different numbers for the populations, by all means throw them up.<br /> <br /> Also, at least according to one of the scenarios, just what's in the Revised books should count, and so I don't think Arch-Mages are even considered since I don't think they are covered in the book.<br /> Another thought: if you do include the other Changing Breeds alongside the Garou, the outcome changes a lot I think (as does their numbers). As was stated, the Garou were only ever meant to be soldiers. Having the support Gaia meant for them makes all the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>As-is, there is one option left to really fuck their enemies over, though. It comes from the most unlikely place, too...<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got a labrys.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got a grand klaive.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got launch codes for cruise missiles.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Hatred-of-Apes, what do you have?&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_COcHHvte-0\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I got a rock.&quot;</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T16:35:36-07:00","id":638446,"title":"","content":"I think you'll find Sam Haight wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T17:05:23-07:00","id":638488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638446#post638446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you'll find Sam Haight wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, the ashtray? How does a knicknack beat the Antediluvians or Avatars of the Incarna or even a rinky-dink Archmage? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T18:44:19-07:00","id":638621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638339#post638339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Masters of the Art</i> it's THE book on Archmages, and it' from (early) Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite aware of the book. In &quot;Scenario A&quot; The OP specified Revised Core books which I believe doesn't have anything to say on Arch Mages. Also, with only considering tradition mages and no technocracy or Marauders and Nephandi, I would say it cuts down the Mages chances a lot.<br /> <br /> For &quot;Scenario B&quot;, everybody....the fight doesn't matter since it includes too many beings whose power is undefinable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638367#post638367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey Hatred-of-Apes, what do you have?&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_COcHHvte-0\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I got a rock.&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This was very amusing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T20:45:49-07:00","id":638768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638367#post638367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As-is, there is one option left to really fuck their enemies over, though. It comes from the most unlikely place, too...<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got a labrys.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got a grand klaive.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got launch codes for cruise missiles.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Hatred-of-Apes, what do you have?&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_COcHHvte-0\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I got a rock.&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The OP stated as sole rule to not break Earth or extinct humanity, so no meteor. It will be either too much or not enough, unless a werewolf make Mage-and-Vampire-Hunting-Primium-Meteor. On Flames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T21:16:31-07:00","id":638786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638768#post638768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP stated as sole rule to not break Earth or extinct humanity, so no meteor. It will be either too much or not enough, unless a werewolf make Mage-and-Vampire-Hunting-Primium-Meteor. On Flames.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think enough humans would survive. You can always ask Rorg to toss smaller meteors. Enough to just obliterate a city or country. In any case, Humanity on the whole would survive in some capacity. And end up in a state some Garou would actually prefer, having their numbers reduced and infrastructure fractured.<br /> This was actually kind of my point earlier, in the Garou asking their allies and patrons for help. I don't think even an Ante would do well fighting against avatars (yes, multiple) of Helios. And with a war like this, that would be a very real possibility.<br /> The description of a war like this would essentially be the Apocalypse from the Garou point of view. There would be nothing left to lose, and they would go all out. They may or may not win, but there is certainly the possibility of victory.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T21:38:54-07:00","id":638800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638786#post638786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think enough humans would survive. You can always ask Rorg to toss smaller meteors. Enough to just obliterate a city or country. In any case, Humanity on the whole would survive in some capacity. And end up in a state some Garou would actually prefer, having their numbers reduced and infrastructure fractured.<br /> This was actually kind of my point earlier, in the Garou asking their allies and patrons for help. I don't think even an Ante would do well fighting against avatars (yes, multiple) of Helios. And with a war like this, that would be a very real possibility.<br /> The description of a war like this would essentially be the Apocalypse from the Garou point of view. There would be nothing left to lose, and they would go all out. They may or may not win, but there is certainly the possibility of victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Helios is a Celestine, so his Avatars would all be roughly on par with Incarnae, and thus able to fry a clan founder from existence easily. Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion is the Incarna of the Sun, specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T22:01:28-07:00","id":638811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638800#post638800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Helios is a Celestine, so his Avatars would all be roughly on par with Incarnae, and thus able to fry a clan founder from existence easily. Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion is the Incarna of the Sun, specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was kind of the point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I have heard a Vampire fan argue that an Incarna isn't as strong as an Antediluvian though, which is why i specifically brought up the idea of multiples of them.<br /> Side note: I always thought Katanka-Sonnak and Hyperion were separate Avatars of Helios. Not that it really makes any difference to this conversation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:19:06-07:00","id":638846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638811#post638811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was kind of the point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I have heard a Vampire fan argue that an Incarna isn't as strong as an Antediluvian though, which is why i specifically brought up the idea of multiples of them.<br /> Side note: I always thought Katanka-Sonnak and Hyperion were separate Avatars of Helios. Not that it really makes any difference to this conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you have a newspaper on hand when they said those things, so as to give them the appropriate Tommy Lee Jones reaction face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T01:54:43-07:00","id":638878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite aware of the book. In &quot;Scenario A&quot; The OP specified Revised Core books which I believe doesn't have anything to say on Arch Mages. Also, with only considering tradition mages and no technocracy or Marauders and Nephandi, I would say it cuts down the Mages chances a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that rule of three, vampires wouldn't be able to use &quot;elder level&quot; disciplines (they're not in the core), and Garou would be limmited to the fetishes/Gifts that appear in the basic (I'm not sure if Garou can employ spirits, if nothing outside the physical world it's permitted). I don't think that it would cut Mage's chances THAT much.<br /> <br /> If anything, it would beneffit Humanity. I think that humanity can *take* most of what the Revised Cores can throw to them (no earth shattering powers in any of the Cores, if I remember well, exept maybe Forces 5), and actually win the war against the monsters, using sheer numbers and high-tech weaponry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-25-2015, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T06:49:48-07:00","id":639054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=638878#post638878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With that rule of three, vampires wouldn't be able to use &quot;elder level&quot; disciplines (they're not in the core), and Garou would be limmited to the fetishes/Gifts that appear in the basic (I'm not sure if Garou can employ spirits, if nothing outside the physical world it's permitted). I don't think that it would cut Mage's chances THAT much.<br /> <br /> If anything, it would beneffit Humanity. I think that humanity can *take* most of what the Revised Cores can throw to them (no earth shattering powers in any of the Cores, if I remember well, exept maybe Forces 5), and actually win the war against the monsters, using sheer numbers and high-tech weaponry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>fair enough, though those weren't my (mostly arbitrary) limitations on the scenario. I think this entire discussion is more than a bit silly since outside of the actual end of the world, this proposed war couldn't really be a consideration. Even with the end of the world, these factions wouldn't team up.<br /> <br /> Also, I've always given humanity a lot more credit than other players I've talked to. There is little reason why regular old humans can't kill some of the world's oldest supernatural monsters. Especially nowadays with modern warfare technology. For example, I've never used the Technocracy to take down [Ravnos]. Humans can, and should have done that without supernatural aid. The only reason to include the Technocracy if for crossover fluff, which isn't necessary to a (solely) Vampire game.<br /> In general, I prefer not to have one game's Big Bad get killed off by another line entirely. It takes away from the event in my opinion. Similar happened with Baba Yaga, where she/it was introduced as a WtA big bad, and was killed off screen by a mystery Vampire monster. There isn't any reason not to let a heroic pack of Garou track her down, and fight their way to her, and finally kill her off. It's anticlimactic to just have one of these antagonists die for &quot;reasons&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-25-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T19:20:31-07:00","id":639708,"title":"","content":"Just for the record, in Baba Yaga's case it wasn't an off-screen kill. It was on-screen, but in a Vampire book.<br /> <br /> What's rather a moot point, since she wasn't killed by PCs either. It could have make for a good crossover, though. Anyone PC killing her would be better.<br /> <br /> And as I said, humanity survives in scenario A. I don't say they win simply because they weren't presented as an option by OP.<br /> <br /> Scenario B still takes out the world, because too much things fighting all-out. Unless the Incarnae can track down every vampire on Earth, deal with every Discipline (including the ones that can actually protect against the sun) and not commit a LOT of collateral damage, I wouldn't say their victory AND humanity's survival is a given, even only over vampires.<br /> <br /> This discussion was too obviously completely silly from the start, we're arguing about total nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T21:04:58-07:00","id":639830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=639708#post639708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, in Baba Yaga's case it wasn't an off-screen kill. It was on-screen, but in a Vampire book.<br /> <br /> What's rather a moot point, since she wasn't killed by PCs either. It could have make for a good crossover, though. Anyone PC killing her would be better.<br /> <br /> And as I said, humanity survives in scenario A. I don't say they win simply because they weren't presented as an option by OP.<br /> <br /> Scenario B still takes out the world, because too much things fighting all-out. Unless the Incarnae can track down every vampire on Earth, deal with every Discipline (including the ones that can actually protect against the sun) and not commit a LOT of collateral damage, I wouldn't say their victory AND humanity's survival is a given, even only over vampires.<br /> <br /> This discussion was too obviously completely silly from the start, we're arguing about total nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am actually in almost total agreement with all of this.<br /> <br /> I don't actually think any discipline that protects against the sun is going to help against an Incarna. Using Hyperion as the example...the fact that he is a Sun Incarna is only part of what makes him so dangerous (to Vampires). He is also an Incarna embodying rebirth and renewal. It is entirely possible that he could use a power which simulates the Gift renew the Cycle (Silverfang Rank 6) to instant slay any vampire. Technically, the rank 6 Gift would emulate this exact sort of power that an Incarna can do naturally. Also, like any God, he has many facets...Hyperion can be a fierce warrior...or diplomat or oracle or anything else. Basically, Celestines and their Incarna can do anything needed. They are the &quot;Plot Device&quot; beings of the Werewolf cosmology. And in a Werewolf game, you can actually just take a trip and go talk to them (not saying it's super easy, but easier than finding equivalent beings in Vampire for sure, and arguably easier than doing so would be for a Mage).<br /> <br /> Anyway, discussing silly nonsense is part of what the internet and forums is all about. As long as everyone is respectful and enjoying themselves, it's fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T22:33:49-07:00","id":639877,"title":"","content":"Clearly, the war goes to whoever can get an audience with the Unconquered Sun for long enough to get him to look away from the Cosmic X-Box and deal with all this shit.<br /> <br /> So Werewolves or Mages.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T22:54:38-07:00","id":639883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=639877#post639877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, the war goes to whoever can get an audience with the Unconquered Sun for long enough to get him to look away from the Cosmic X-Box and deal with all this shit.<br /> <br /> So Werewolves or Mages.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is an extremely different setting, the branch point possibly being when the Sidereals actually did something instead of just drowning their frustrations in heavenly blow and courtesan gods. In any case, what goes on in Exalted doesn't determine much of anything in classic WoD, unlike the old relationship between Earthdawn and Shadowrun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T20:54:22-07:00","id":641047,"title":"","content":"Exalted tried to be the Earthdawn of cWoD, but then the authors concluded it was better going for its own.<br /> <br /> Incarnae are god-like and full of plot-devices, but so are Methuselahs. A 5th gen can have almost any effect for its Disciplines. And by the <u>few, loose and sometimes contradictory</u> rules for crossovers, a Xth rank Gift user can be countered at a Clash of Wills by a Xth level Discipline and is automatically countered by a higher level Discipline (counting the level of the user in the Discipline, not the level it can achieve or the level of the actual power in the Discipline). By myself, I would put Incarnae between Ranks 5 and 7. So a Methuselah of 5th gen could surpass them in its highest level Discipline. And being Methuselah, they could have a good variety of powers for each Discipline level beyond 5, so a power able to at least have a chance with an Incarna would make sense. More for 4th gens. For 3rd gen, Ravnos actually resisted four days of direct sun before being hit by whatever actually killed him, and we can argue ad aeternum about the death.<br /> <br /> And doesn't mater if it is easier to contact an Incarna, the Methuselahs would be there.<br /> <br /> Because it is <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4WgT9gy4zQA\" target=\"_blank\">THE ULTIMATE SHOWDOWN OF ULTIMATE DESTINY</a></b>!!!<br /> <br /> So, yes, I think a Discipline that protect against the sun can protect against an Incarna if used by a skilled enough Metuselah, together with the other protective powers this Methuselah could have, all that being a lot of assumption for both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T04:03:14-07:00","id":641350,"title":"","content":"Comparing an insignificant being with limited powers like a Methuselah against an Incarna it's like comparing an ant with an elephant.<br /> <br /> Note that 8th level powers are defined, and most, if not all, can theoretically be defeated by normal werewolves with normal buffs (they're ruled, and new &quot;invented&quot; powers of the same level shouldn't be more powerful than written ones). The powers of the Incarna, in contrast, are explicitly beyond character sheets. A mere Rank 6 has nothing in front of the true form of an Incarna.<br /> A Rank 6 it's merely a legendary hero, and also can be (theoretically) defeated with all and her (powerful, but stated) Rank 6th Gifts. However, its explicitly stated that an Incarna can't be defeated without plot devices or powerful allies aka. <i>Storiteller's Fiat</i>.<br /> <br /> Think that Rank 6 Gift it's needed to summon the avatar of an Incarna which it's much weaker than it's true form. An avatar it's a mere fragment of the Incarna, and yet they usually have Attributes on 20+ (and almost limitless magic). How many Methuselah have you seen with Attributes at 20+. And remember that that those character sheets with 20-25 in Attributes (like the Fenris Avatar, or the Aeon in the Book of Madness) are mere slivers of the true power of the Incarna.<br /> <br /> An Incarna it's easily on the power level of an Antediluvian, if only because they both fall into the narrative plot device category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-27-2015, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:42:32-07:00","id":641417,"title":"","content":"Everything Aleph said. 100%","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T07:35:40-07:00","id":641536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=641417#post641417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything Aleph said. 100%</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one quibble - while most Rank 6 Gifts are very useful, I would hesitate to call too many of them powerful. Dance of Shiva, now there's a powerful Rank 6 Gift. Admittedly, for the Nagah, but it can theoretically cover the world in a sea of magical flames if the user has an appropriate Performance specialty in dance and spends a Willpower point for a bonus success (radius approaches 6000 miles, which is nearly double that of the Earth). The flames, at the point where the fire spreads out the widest, will also deal 21 dice of aggravated damage. Now that's powerful. Renew the Cycle doesn't quite measure up, especially since Dance of Shiva doesn't cost a damn thing to use, except the consequences of your actions, and in particular dancing for a full minute plus three seconds. Shield of Gaia, similarly, is apparently something that can get bumped down to level five for some Fera (Shield of C'et, in case anyone was wondering).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:08:36-07:00","id":641780,"title":"","content":"It's a war between Garou, vampires and mages. No incarns and no spirits. Altought garou and mages could summon spirits, let's say that any spirit much more powerful than the casterr itself wouldn't even botter getting into the fight.<br /> Yes, we can consider every power even those who aren't in the core books. I just don't want to consider other beings or entities/instituitions (no incarna, no tecnocracy)<br /> In scenario (B) we can consider antes (and caine) since they are vampires that are present in the core books as playable clans.<br /> Humans could also be one of the parties, but i thought that they wouldnt even know what is really going on besides a lit of crazy events.<br /> Seems by the answers that mages are winning.<br /> <br /> And i think that caine is being overlooked. He not only can create any power he wants, he is cursed in a way that anyone who harms him will suffer sevenfold.<br /> How much archmages there is? I think that there are more low gen vampires than high power mages.<br /> And without spirit or entities help the garou seem screwed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T10:28:51-07:00","id":641796,"title":"","content":"Your guidelines are quite arbitrary. You do realise there are Garou Gifts that allow them to summon avatars? Denying rites and spirit pacts and is kinda like disallowing thaumaturgy and ghouls. The Antedullivans and Caine are in the same nebulous plot device territory as the Incarnae,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T11:08:23-07:00","id":641832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=641780#post641780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a war between Garou, vampires and mages. No incarns and no spirits. Altought garou and mages could summon spirits, let's say that any spirit much more powerful than the casterr itself wouldn't even botter getting into the fight.<br /> Yes, we can consider every power even those who aren't in the core books. I just don't want to consider other beings or entities/instituitions (no incarna, no tecnocracy)<br /> In scenario (B) we can consider antes (and caine) since they are vampires that are present in the core books as playable clans.<br /> Humans could also be one of the parties, but i thought that they wouldnt even know what is really going on besides a lit of crazy events.<br /> Seems by the answers that mages are winning.<br /> <br /> And i think that caine is being overlooked. He not only can create any power he wants, he is cursed in a way that anyone who harms him will suffer sevenfold.<br /> How much archmages there is? I think that there are more low gen vampires than high power mages.<br /> And without spirit or entities help the garou seem screwed</div> </div> </div> </div>These are really kind of arbitrary rules. Should Garou packs and Septs not have totem spirits then as well?<br /> <br /> When it comes down to it, the answer of who would win is whoever you want, especially if you set up rules like this to ensure who [I]can[/] win. Caine's powers don't matter. Archmage powers don't matter. They can all do whatever you (whoever is writing the story) wants them to be able to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T11:52:54-07:00","id":641914,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I didn't knew that there are gifts that summon incarna. In this case they should count.<br /> It is not arbitrary, I'm just considering the protagonists of each system (and in (B), the most powerful ones). I don't know werewolf very well. So if a pc could do it in a game (gifts, etc.) then it's on.<br /> I just didn't wanted garou calling gaia or anyone calling godlike entities to help. My knowledge of garou and spirits is pretty small","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T12:35:38-07:00","id":641942,"title":"","content":"All of these sorts of questions are arbitrary, pitting three massive (and often incompatible) settings against one another will not result in any meaningful conclusions. Hell, just pitting Mage against itself is confusing enough, given the immense thematic breadth of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T12:42:24-07:00","id":641950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=641914#post641914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I didn't knew that there are gifts that summon incarna. In this case they should count.<br /> It is not arbitrary, I'm just considering the protagonists of each system (and in (B), the most powerful ones). I don't know werewolf very well. So if a pc could do it in a game (gifts, etc.) then it's on.<br /> I just didn't wanted garou calling gaia or anyone calling godlike entities to help. My knowledge of garou and spirits is pretty small</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the Garou did, Gaia would be virtually certain to not help them with direct action, and possibly not even with an immediate and concrete response. The scale of Gaia is, though hotly debated, somewhere between beyond a Celestine and beyond everything encompassing the entire universe. Calling upon such a vast figure for aid is likely to get a very big picture kind of boost, such as fertility increasing or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:17:13-07:00","id":642008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=641914#post641914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I didn't knew that there are gifts that summon incarna. In this case they should count.<br /> It is not arbitrary, I'm just considering the protagonists of each system (and in (B), the most powerful ones). I don't know werewolf very well. So if a pc could do it in a game (gifts, etc.) then it's on.<br /> I just didn't wanted garou calling gaia or anyone calling godlike entities to help. My knowledge of garou and spirits is pretty small</div> </div> </div> </div>Rite of Summoning, a level 2 Rite can potentially summon Incarna and Celestine Avatar. Incarna are dif 8-9, Celestine Avatars are dif 10. For every hour spent invoking the Spirit, the dif drops by 1 to a minimum of 3. Successes rolled determine the attitude of the Spirit when it arrives. At least 3 successes is preferred for a Neutral start to the encounter.<br /> <br /> To sum up my point: a starting character who spends a few hours on the rite has a decent chance of summoning a Celestine Avatar to show up and be neutral (perhaps even friendly). <u>Every</u> caern (and most packs) should have a of Garou able to perform this (fairly simple) Rite.<br /> <br /> Now this isn't to say that this is (or even could be) a repeatable tactic for Garou. I was just wanting to point out something they can do which could certainly help them in an all out War/The Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-27-2015, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T16:18:25-07:00","id":643531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=641417#post641417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything Aleph said. 100%</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted, if not entirely convinced, given that the power level of a Methuselah is still beyond a Rank 6 Fera in mystic potency. Even if the Incarna can have far more dice and versatility, it says nothing about mystic potency, and its effect on defensive powers. But this is as much as I can say, since the rules weren't meant to cover this issue.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the rules are arbitrary. Or, at least, not clear enough.<br /> <br /> I can actually think of spirits not taking part because, sure, they're not Fera themselves and there are no reason to really think they see themselves as fighting side-by-side with the Fera. If spirits where allowed to fight by themselves, someone could argue that a lot of Wyrm spirits would show up to help the vampires.<br /> <br /> But while Vampire and Mage lines are self-contained in a sense, Werewolf don't work without spirits. You took from the game the very beings that occupy the niche for Methuselahs and Archmages. By the way, you can take Caine together, because he isn't even necessarily a vampire.<br /> <br /> Yes, on high-end level of power Werewolf got the short straw, but because its main villain is a spirit, and other werewolves are meant for rivals, not too-powerful-for-this-world opponents. Mage and Vampire both places the same splat as tpftw opponents and main villains.<br /> <br /> Oh, and humanity WILL know everything because you FREAKING BET IT ALL! Even in scenario A this will escalate to world-shattering levels. In scenario B it will end truly only when humanity is no more. And probably no one else.<br /> <br /> Vampires are going to do well, because numbers, resources, and everything up to 4th generation can be used in scenario A. Mages are going to obliterate the opposition anyway and probably half of them are going to spontaneously die of too much Paradox, a lot of others crippled for life. The splat still win. Werewolves are meant to work with spirits, so if you simply take the spirits from them, they're dead. With spirits they have the upper hand over vampires.<br /> <br /> Maybe reducing that to only starting characters with no freebies? Then I think we can have some barely meaningful discussion. Otherwise we're just throwing unverifiable arguments about things never meant to interact by the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T19:22:12-07:00","id":643696,"title":"","content":"Again, werewolves can use spirits that they are capable of controling. Let's not count super motherfucker badasses spirits that won't give a crap about werewolves and what they are asking.<br /> Now, what about antediluvians and mathusalens with blood magic (Ur-shulgi?) against mages and archmages? Could they do something about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:05:17-07:00","id":643757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=643696#post643696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Again, werewolves can use spirits that they are capable of controling. Let's not count super motherfucker badasses spirits that won't give a crap about werewolves and what they are asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part though, the Garou do not control spirits. They live in a symbiotic relationship. and there are at least 13 &quot;super motherfucker badasses spirits&quot; that will absolutely care about the Garou and what they are asking. The Tribal Incarna (not to mention the Celestial Incarna that serve as patrons for each tribe). Now adding to that, any and all Septs can rely on Spirits to aid in their defense. Caerns are sacred places, to the Gaoru and to the Spirits that frequent them. Every pack has a totem spirit as well, and the pack spirit has been known to fight by the pack's side. The totem of a pack that has been together a long while can grow quite powerful.<br /> There are totems that are more than likely capable of counter magic. Any powerful spirit that has magic as a spiritual correspondence may (and I do emphasize may, Mage magic isn't covered really in Werewolf) be able to counter and undo magic. Hell, the Uktena (Tribe) actually have a reputation for being able to do so.<br /> This is part of why this scenario is more than a bit silly. the systems weren't meant to crossover like this, so at best you might have rough guidelines on how they could. But certainly there are no rules on how the upper power levels of each game would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=643696#post643696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, what about antediluvians and mathusalens with blood magic (Ur-shulgi?) against mages and archmages? Could they do something about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Make up whatever you want and that's how old blood magic will interact with mage magics. Hell, the only reason [Ravnos] survived what he did is because someone wrote the story that way. Not because it was possible to roll out the scene and see.<br /> <br /> This will be the same answer for any and all Arch-Mage/Ante/Caine/Celestine/Incarna/Celestine interactions. You cannot get any &quot;true&quot; answers for this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T22:12:35-07:00","id":643760,"title":"","content":"You know, I don't really think that you can take any Gift as reflective of a spirit's power as such. They're weird things that spirits bequeath to Garou and Fera even if the spirit in question has no Charm pertaining to the effect in question. It gets weird. Even weirder when you consider that Garou don't learn Gift of the Porcupine until Rank 4, but Rokea get an equivalent, Teeth of the Skin, as a pick for starting Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=643531#post643531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noted, if not entirely convinced, given that the power level of a Methuselah is still beyond a Rank 6 Fera in mystic potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seriously doubt that. Vampire has to rig things heavily to make that the case in its crossover rules, comparing Traits that have no direct relation to Discipline levels for both Werewolf and Mage. Compare Discipline to Rank? Sphere rating? How about we use Rage/Gnosis and Arete instead, respectively; those actually make sense. In some cases, you might want to reference permanent Renown for Garou and Fera, since that provides the oomph for a few Gifts - Trick Shot, Fu Xi's Honor, and lots of rewritten Fera Gifts from W20 CB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T08:30:57-07:00","id":644172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, werewolves can use spirits that they are capable of controling. Let's not count super motherfucker badasses spirits that won't give a crap about werewolves and what they are asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <b>idpersona</b> said, and I add: it is the same as limiting vampires to the methuselahs they can actually summon.<br /> <br /> Werewolf's core book have all the rules you need for spirits for a reason. The game IS supposed to work with them. More than Vampire and Mage was ever supposed to work with their upper-end powers.<br /> <br /> Vampire was supposed to work with PCs up to 8th generation. More powerful vampires are a possibility, and completely covered by the rules on core alone, even to some degree the Antediluvian bunch themselves. But that's simply because the core rules are the same for all vampires, what changes is just the Discipline level beyond 5, and even this is debatable, because since such powers are customized, anyway, you can simply make your own all the way up to 10th level. So the core book alone have everything you need for all of those vampires. But they AREN'T meant for the same role. A PC isn't meant to ever have access to Disciplines over 5 unless under the most extraordinary circumstances. Elders are meant as powerful patrons and enemies. Methuselah are meant as godlike beings of legend, to only make an appearance on the background and remain as unfathomable threats and (un)living plot-devices. Antediluvian are meant as the very gods of old, they are the forces behind the end of the world of the vampires.<br /> <br /> So we are working, first and foremost, with literary roles here: Protagonists, Patrons, God-lings and World-Enders. In vampire you have the same class of creature occupying all those roles, under mostly the same rules, but PCs aren't supposed to leave the first role easily, and even less to ever leave the second role.<br /> <br /> In Mage you have mostly the same rule covering it all, again, with one distinction: PCs ARE meant to be able to cover it all. You could say that Masters are meant for the role of Patrons, while an Archmage of &quot;lesser&quot; power is a God-ling, and he greatest Archmages are World-Enders. Except, first, that the world wasn't supposed to end in Mage. Second, that not only the roles are covered by the same rules, now they are truly meant for PCs. Nothing can stop a successful PC from covering all the way up to Arete 10 and Spheres 9. No tricky Diablerie or anything. What hold Earth's power level <u>currently</u> is a prerogative of setting: in Revised, the game starts with no Archmage and almost no Master on Earth. But it simply isn't a rule, just a momentary hold in the setting. Its just a mater of time until Earth is filled with Archmasters of untold power again. Of course, you don't actually have Spheres beyond Master level in the core, but it follows the same guidelines for Disciplines, and what's more: Mages don't really need them at all. 5 is more than enough for them to break the world apart.<br /> <br /> Then we get to Werewolf, and that's the thing: while Vampire and Mage were supposed to work with the same general creatures for every role, the Fera are supposed to work with spirits <b><u>all the freaking time!</u></b> The Fera themselves are supposed to occupy the roles of Protagonists and, for the Rank 5 and 6, Patrons. And spirits are supposed to occupy them all. They aren't just powers for the Garou. The werecreatures walk among spirits, talk with spirits, negotiate with spirits, and bargain for spirit's aid all the time. They aren't supposed to work without spirits, nor even to only have spiritual help through their own powers. Heck, one of the most basic plots in Werewolf is the spirit-quest, where PCs from any Rank can find and bargain with spirits far more powerful than themselves. As was said before, it is as if a starting Vampire PC could just go talk with Mithras, the 4th gen Prince of London, and actually expect not only to be heard, but to be granted a boon. It is almost unthinkable (if possible, yes) for a vampire, and exceedingly hard for a Mage, but actually common for the Fera. Like, most Rank 1 Fera will encounter such beings before they achieve Rank 2. A lot encountered <u>before</u> Rank 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, what about antediluvians and mathusalens with blood magic (Ur-shulgi?) against mages and archmages? Could they do something about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the principle that having near infinite variety of static power equals having dynamic power, yes, they could. As <b>idpersona</b> said, you can do whatever you want at this level, pretty much. I would argue that the vampires have the upper hand here, but based solely on the rule of mystic potency I referenced: there are very few Mages at levels 8 or 9 of Spheres, and no one at level 10. So the Antes get the upper hand over everyone else in potency, while the Methuselah have no superiors, only equals.<br /> <br /> But there are other factors. One is that vampires only get such dynamism on extremely high-level cases, and <u>only</u> for NPCs. PCs are bound to static powers because, in this case, dynamic powers are acquired with age. Even characters like Tremere (before or after losing his body, doesn't mater) and Augustus Giovanni wouldn't be privy to dynamism, because they are too young for such mastery of untold powers. Mages have dynamism from start, so we aren't talking only about the power-players, but about every single Mage.<br /> <br /> Not possible at all to say who would win at this level. Both sides can shatter nations with a thought, continents with a little more effort. Both can do whatever the writer wants them to do. Stalemate, there are no solution, except the certainty that humanity can't survive such powers on the lose with so much blood in the eyes.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear on it again, the rules weren't meant for crossover at all from scratch, and actually neither meant to truly cover high-ends. To try a crossover of high-ends is to push them well beyond what they can actually account for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I don't really think that you can take any Gift as reflective of a spirit's power as such. They're weird things that spirits bequeath to Garou and Fera even if the spirit in question has no Charm pertaining to the effect in question. It gets weird. Even weirder when you consider that Garou don't learn Gift of the Porcupine until Rank 4, but Rokea get an equivalent, Teeth of the Skin, as a pick for starting Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, for sure. But we need a parameter to argue anything. Given the complete lack of rules to cover the issue, we can only speculate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously doubt that. Vampire has to rig things heavily to make that the case in its crossover rules, comparing Traits that have no direct relation to Discipline levels for both Werewolf and Mage. Compare Discipline to Rank? Sphere rating? How about we use Rage/Gnosis and Arete instead, respectively; those actually make sense. In some cases, you might want to reference permanent Renown for Garou and Fera, since that provides the oomph for a few Gifts - Trick Shot, Fu Xi's Honor, and lots of rewritten Fera Gifts from W20 CB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't really remember if I saw those rules on more than one book, but I'm almost sure that I did. Either way, official crossover rules, give or take. I don't think they're good, nor that they were done with caution. I actually think they're just a half-assed patch done hastily when they had no other option but finally make crossover rules, lest their buildings be invaded by angry mobs of fans. But those are the rule we have. The potency of any mystic effect is defined by: level of the vampire in the Discipline, level of the Mage in the highest Sphere requirement of the effect, Rank of the Fera, period. It <u>does</u> make some sense, and I don't see Rage or Gnosis working better. Renown, maybe, it would be a better start, for sure. But in the end, again, we're trying to argue with basis on three distinct system that weren't meant to work together.<br /> <br /> Maybe 4th edition gives us something we can really work with. Until then...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T09:06:34-07:00","id":644281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644172#post644172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the principle that having near infinite variety of static power equals having dynamic power, yes, they could. As <b>idpersona</b> said, you can do whatever you want at this level, pretty much. I would argue that the vampires have the upper hand here, but based solely on the rule of mystic potency I referenced: there are very few Mages at levels 8 or 9 of Spheres, and no one at level 10. So the Antes get the upper hand over everyone else in potency, while the Methuselah have no superiors, only equals.<br /> <br /> But there are other factors. One is that vampires only get such dynamism on extremely high-level cases, and <u>only</u> for NPCs. PCs are bound to static powers because, in this case, dynamic powers are acquired with age. Even characters like Tremere (before or after losing his body, doesn't mater) and Augustus Giovanni wouldn't be privy to dynamism, because they are too young for such mastery of untold powers. Mages have dynamism from start, so we aren't talking only about the power-players, but about every single Mage.<br /> <br /> Not possible at all to say who would win at this level. Both sides can shatter nations with a thought, continents with a little more effort. Both can do whatever the writer wants them to do. Stalemate, there are no solution, except the certainty that humanity can't survive such powers on the lose with so much blood in the eyes.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear on it again, the rules weren't meant for crossover at all from scratch, and actually neither meant to truly cover high-ends. To try a crossover of high-ends is to push them well beyond what they can actually account for.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the advantage of the static power is no paradox and no consensus. And an methusela or ante have &quot;dynamic&quot; power without this limitation. Ur-Shulgi could create a ritual to block the fucking sun without any problem, while an archmage making rain fire would get serious problems with paradox and disbilief to the point where the effect itself could be undone, am i right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T09:58:43-07:00","id":644364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the principle that having near infinite variety of static power equals having dynamic power, yes, they could. As <b>idpersona</b>said, you can do whatever you want at this level, pretty much. I would argue that the vampires have the upper hand here, but based solely on the rule of mystic potency I referenced: there are very few Mages at levels 8 or 9 of Spheres, and no one at level 10. So the Antes get the upper hand over everyone else in potency, while the Methuselah have no superiors, only equals.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a detail. Actually, there are mages with Spheres at level 10.<br /> <br /> Exemplars are supposed to reach to that power eventually (it's in the Exemplar section of Masters Of The Art), and no rule says you can't reach them with xp (Al-Aswad did in his end-world scenario, albeit that's not canon, just like all end world scenarios), even when their power it's left outside the books.<br /> <br /> And the magical potency rules are canon, but not alone. You can use<i> success based determinism</i>, for instance, that it's an official rule too. I don't think that Discipline level should be taken in count to have a notion of the power of beings that haven't powers that go up to 10 (or that haven't numbers at all).<br /> <br /> Appart from that, yeah I kinda agree.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the advantage of the static power is no paradox and no consensus. And an methusela or ante have &quot;dynamic&quot; power without this limitation.Ur-Shulgi could create a ritual to block the fucking sun without any problem, while an archmage making rain fire would get serious problems with paradox and disbilief to the point where the effect itself could be undone, am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either he has already created that ritual, or he will have to spend years to create one. A mage has Paradox, </span></span>but can create such a ritual on the spot <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">(and, of course, vampires running through the street will likely mess up the Consensus. There's no Paradox if most people ends believing in magic) .<br /> <br /> The &quot;dynamism&quot; of the elders it's merely a form of Storyteller's prerogative (</span></span>in a sense, all thaumaturges have it<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">). Just as it's deciding what crossover rules to use (or who wins in an Ur-Shulgi vs Fenris vs hypothetical Archmage, for the case). </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-29-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T10:33:07-07:00","id":644399,"title":"","content":"I've never been a fan of the &quot;Magical Potency Rule&quot;.<br /> By the magical potency rule logic (as applied above) , 4th gen Vampires are better than God (the one that cursed Caine) since he/she/it doesn't have a declared power level above 9. That sort of logic falls flat fairly quick.<br /> Even just on in game rules. A Vampire with a discipline (any of them) at 6 is <u>not</u> more powerful <i>mystically</i> than a Mage with Spheres of 5. This is certainly false.<br /> <br /> In a Dark Ages game, you can have a starting Vampire with a level 6 Discipline. This rule then posits that said (starting) character has more mystical might than a Mage character with Arete 10 and all Spheres at 5. Even if someone thought something was good enough idea to publish as a rule, you do need to use at least a bit of common sense when choosing to use said rule.<br /> <br /> I seem to remember the Magical Potency rule appearing mostly in Vampire books (or at least first appearing in them), and crossover rules tend to favor the line they come from. That's because if you are playing a Vampire game, you aren't supposed to be overshadowed by other Supernaturals. I seem to remember a rule that showed up in Werewolf for crossover that said that Garou could countermagic Mages Spheres using Gnosis. That makes no sense, and so shouldn't be used in any game, never mind a game with Mage players. Saying you need Mind 5 to stand a change at resisting Dominate 5 is dumb.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T11:24:04-07:00","id":644443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644281#post644281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the advantage of the static power is no paradox and no consensus. And an methusela or ante have &quot;dynamic&quot; power without this limitation. Ur-Shulgi could create a ritual to block the fucking sun without any problem, while an archmage making rain fire would get serious problems with paradox and disbilief to the point where the effect itself could be undone, am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, given that you declared that they're out for one another's blood at all costs, this is a moot point. The Archmage will do it anyway, because Fuck the Paradox. Second, the actual effects for those to be accomplished, including time and successes, are completely out of rules by now. They are able to do whatever you want them to do, the Archmage included.<br /> <br /> Hell, a Prime Archmage can even make Ur-Shulgi get his Paradox!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of the &quot;Magical Potency Rule&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do I. Hell, I'm not a fan of it even inside Vampire. The idea that you have no chance against a power, even with the proper counter-power, unless you have it at the same or greater level... it is utterly nonsense for me. I like nWoD rules for Clash of Wills, where you get a roll every time, and the greater power simply gives you advantage on the roll.<br /> <br /> BUT, we have to stick to some official rule here. Unless you present a better one, what we have is &quot;Magical Potency&quot;. Success Based Determinism could be a way, if you present how to apply it in this case, through official means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:18:43-07:00","id":644566,"title":"","content":"While it's a bit off topic, if we're comparing Gifts and Disciplines in power level, it would probably make the most sense to compare the level of the Discipline with the level of the Gift. So a level 4 Gift beats a vampire with 3 levels of some Discipline or 3 levels of a Mage's Sphere for that matter. Of the three main OWod creatures, only mages really have a universal power stat, Ar\u00eate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:52:25-07:00","id":644607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644566#post644566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's a bit off topic, if we're comparing Gifts and Disciplines in power level, it would probably make the most sense to compare the level of the Discipline with the level of the Gift. So a level 4 Gift beats a vampire with 3 levels of some Discipline or 3 levels of a Mage's Sphere for that matter. Of the three main OWod creatures, only mages really have a universal power stat, Ar\u00eate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gift levels vary depending on who's learning it. Their effectiveness remains the same, but Ananasi can learn their equivalent of Icy Chill of Despair as a starting Gift. Shadow Lords learn it as a Rank 3 Gift, and in the end, it's roughly on par with Presence 5, but isn't on all the time. In return for requiring activation, a character with an applicable specialty can end up requiring more successes on the Willpower roll to resist her Gift than it's mathematically possible to roll, short of being on par with an Incarna's war avatar, and even then, it would require that most of those 15-20 dice come up as successes, with no 1s.<br /> <br /> And let's mention Shield of Gaia/C'et again. Shield of Gaia is a Rank 6 Gift for Red Talons. For Rokea, Shield of C'et, which differs only in name and required Rank, is level five.<br /> <br /> This doesn't fucking work. It has never worked, and it never will. It's a bad idea to compare Rank of Gifts or their users, plain and simple. Rank is a social position, Gift level is a cost or authorization level, and can vary simply because you're, say, too spiritually attuned to water to learn Blaze Talons at Rank 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:17:23-07:00","id":644618,"title":"","content":"Rank is a socialo position, but Gift level isn't, it is a representation of the power of the Gift. If there are Gifts of different levels for different types of creatures, it may be the case that these are in fact different Gifts (supernaturally, spiritually different) that simply utilize the same rules. Or it could be the case that sources for the Gift might instill more supernatural power into that Gift. Of course, that isn't perfect, but it is the most consistent way of doing it, to compare the level of individual powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:26:23-07:00","id":644623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644618#post644618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank is a socialo position, but Gift level isn't, it is a representation of the power of the Gift. If there are Gifts of different levels for different types of creatures, it may be the case that these are in fact different Gifts (supernaturally, spiritually different) that simply utilize the same rules. Or it could be the case that sources for the Gift might instill more supernatural power into that Gift. Of course, that isn't perfect, but it is the most consistent way of doing it, to compare the level of individual powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Consistent&quot; and &quot;Gift power level&quot; don't go together, ever. This should be a red flag about the kind of comparison you're suggesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T16:28:41-07:00","id":644708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644281#post644281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And an methusela or ante have &quot;dynamic&quot; power without this limitation. Ur-Shulgi could create a ritual to block the fucking sun without any problem, while an archmage making rain fire would get serious problems with paradox and disbilief to the point where the effect itself could be undone, am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually disagree with this assessment even as a base statement. Why is it that you think Methuselahs can make up their own powers whenever they want? And given that it takes Obten 9 to block out the Sun and it specifically concerns itself with darkness, I don\u2019t believe that there can just be a ritual to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644443#post644443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT, we have to stick to some official rule here. Unless you present a better one, what we have is &quot;Magical Potency&quot;. Success Based Determinism could be a way, if you present how to apply it in this case, through official means.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are other \u201cofficial rules\u201d being ignored with this anyways, so why stick to this one? The House of Tremere book present a bunch of crossover rules for Mages and Vampires that are frequently ignored because they make no sense and people think they\u2019re stupid. Should Garou be able to counter Magick using Gnosis. The Werewolf: the Dark Ages book presented a bunch of rules for Werewolf/Vampire crossover that can make Garou near immune to a lot of disciplines with difficulties based on virtues. And again, plenty of people ignore them because they favor the Garou too much. Ignoring rules that don\u2019t make sense in crossover has always been a thing (and should be). Common sense is required. A Mage that can create an entire consciousness from scratch (Mind 5) is more powerful than a 13<sup>th</sup> gen vampire with Dominate 5. This <u>isn\u2019t</u> debatable. And that statement doesn\u2019t even take into account said Mage\u2019s Arete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644607#post644607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't fucking work. It has never worked, and it never will. It's a bad idea to compare Rank of Gifts or their users, plain and simple. Rank is a social position, Gift level is a cost or authorization level, and can vary simply because you're, say, too spiritually attuned to water to learn Blaze Talons at Rank 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644618#post644618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If there are Gifts of different levels for different types of creatures, it may be the case that these are in fact different Gifts (supernaturally, spiritually different) that simply utilize the same rules. Or it could be the case that sources for the Gift might instill more supernatural power into that Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>These statements don\u2019t make sense. You are saying that a rank 4 gift is more powerful than a rank 1 gift even though they do the exact same thing, using the exact same system? That\u2019s the problem exactly\u2026.the Rank of the Gift is determined by the learner\u2019s affinity with said gift. Not by the power of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T02:31:33-07:00","id":645192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=644618#post644618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank is a socialo position, but Gift level isn't, it is a representation of the power of the Gift. If there are Gifts of different levels for different types of creatures, it may be the case that these are in fact different Gifts (supernaturally, spiritually different) that simply utilize the same rules. Or it could be the case that sources for the Gift might instill more supernatural power into that Gift. Of course, that isn't perfect, but it is the most consistent way of doing it, to compare the level of individual powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise that Level 6 gifts are somewhere along Level 8-9 disciplines in their effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T04:16:34-07:00","id":645243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually disagree with this assessment even as a base statement. Why is it that you think Methuselahs can make up their own powers whenever they want? And given that it takes Obten 9 to block out the Sun and it specifically concerns itself with darkness, I don\u2019t believe that there can just be a ritual to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they <u>kind of</u> can. The precise assumption is that a Methuselah probably have enough variety in her powers already for that, and possibly can develop something with an easier time. And rituals can do whatever a discipline can do (what is by itself another problem within the game, by the way). There ARE a ritual to do precisely this same thing, though it is an Abyss Mysticism ritual, but nothing on the game hints at it being impossible for a level 9 ritual of whatever else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other \u201cofficial rules\u201d being ignored with this anyways, so why stick to this one?</div> </div> </div> </div>For no reason, I didn't intended to be sarcastic or something. Just really think we should stick to official rules because common sense have no place in this entire thread. And because common sense IS subjective, and discussions have to stick to objective arguments (even half-assed ones). But you can bring whatever rule not contradicted by Revised.<br /> <br /> If we were talking about actually playing a game, then we could objectively tackle the problems with the crappy rules (or lack thereof. Not to say of the contradictions). But it isn't the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Consistent&quot; and &quot;Gift power level&quot; don't go together, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you ignore the fact that the &quot;Mystic Potency Rule&quot; is a crappy one to begin with (I never said its good. It isn't. Just isn't), it finds a hard time with Werewolfs. Thing is: if you stick the potency to the Gift, you take from the Fera the ability to improve their prowess with such Gift. A Vampire with Obfuscate 3 can increase the resistance of Mask of a Thousand Faces just putting more dots in Obfuscate. It works for all the powers in the Discipline. But Gifts don't work that way, so a level 1 Scent of Man, will be level 1 forever?<br /> <br /> That's why they put it on Rank for Fera. What isn't fair, either. They get even more mystically weak at low level (a starting Vamp can have level 3 easily, 5 with effort. A Mage is almost guaranteed to have a 3), then get advantage at <u>everything</u> until Rank 5 (6 for some awesome dudes), and them get stuck for life.<br /> <br /> Probably Renown would be a better choice, though not the one we officially get for now. And even them I have my doubts. I really think we should get something better than &quot;Mystic Potency&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realise that Level 6 gifts are somewhere along Level 8-9 disciplines in their effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, in that their effects are completely arbitrary and inconsistent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T04:23:14-07:00","id":645274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=645243#post645243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean, in that their effects are completely arbitrary and inconsistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, which is a direct response to Sgt. Brother's comment on how he feels that the power levels should map out straight. And which simply has no basis except someone somewhere doing crossover rules for Vampire and not really bothering to see how other games work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T07:34:01-07:00","id":645393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=645274#post645274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, which is a direct response to Sgt. Brother's comment on how he feels that the power levels should map out straight. And which simply has no basis except someone somewhere doing crossover rules for Vampire and not really bothering to see how other games work.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I find this problem comes up a lot with Mage magick too. How the Mage defends itself (the explanation of Effect) matters a lot more on if it can overcome a power (Discipline or Gift, etc.) than power level comparison. A Mage with Mind 1 or 2 can flat out block pretty much any mental Discipline if they go about things the right way. Saying that because a Vampire has Dominate 4, it can crush a Mage's defense spell, regardless of successes or how it works is just silly.<br /> An example for Garou: there is a Rank 6 gift that can break any bond (material or supernatural). Level 7 Presence cannot overcome it. That just can't be allowed to be a thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, with Gifts and with Magick, the power interactions have to be interpreted based on how they actually function. It is entirely possible for low rank gifts or Sphere 1 or 2 Magick (by level 3 Spheres it is pretty much just a matter of planning accordingly for the situation) to shut down a high level Discipline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:56:47-07:00","id":646953,"title":"","content":"So here is my question about this do mages have to worry about paradox? because if so they will get stomped because either the other supernaturals will get them or paradox will. A single mage could take out a city of vampires with a massive spell, but the backlash would hurt if not kill them.<br /> <br /> With Paradox here are the winners<br /> <br /> Garuo - because they can hide out in the Umbra until the others duke it out and take out the victor<br /> Mages - because they can fight both day and night or bring the day with them into the fight.<br /> Vampires - First to fall because they don't have enough supernatural bite to take out the others<br /> <br /> Without Paradox as a factor <br /> <br /> Mages - because they can give themselves enough time to do whatever they need. <br /> Garuo - even hiding in the umbra its only a matter of time before the mages start coming for them<br /> Vampires - first to fall due to their natural flaws and lack of supernatural bite in comparison to the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":3293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","user":"Rahod","date":". 08-31-2015, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:03:21-07:00","id":663046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/634520-owod-battle-royale?p=645393#post645393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this problem comes up a lot with Mage magick too. How the Mage defends itself (the explanation of Effect) matters a lot more on if it can overcome a power (Discipline or Gift, etc.) than power level comparison. A Mage with Mind 1 or 2 can flat out block pretty much any mental Discipline if they go about things the right way. Saying that because a Vampire has Dominate 4, it can crush a Mage's defense spell, regardless of successes or how it works is just silly.<br /> An example for Garou: there is a Rank 6 gift that can break any bond (material or supernatural). Level 7 Presence cannot overcome it. That just can't be allowed to be a thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, with Gifts and with Magick, the power interactions have to be interpreted based on how they actually function. It is entirely possible for low rank gifts or Sphere 1 or 2 Magick (by level 3 Spheres it is pretty much just a matter of planning accordingly for the situation) to shut down a high level Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... and no.<br /> <br /> The problem is manifold. We have descriptive issues, balance issues, rule issues, and so on. To say that a gift is unbeatable by vampires simply because Werewolf (that don't cover vampires' powers at all) says so isn't more accurate than say that the Discipline will beat the Magick simply because of level (and I would like to remember that it is about level of the user, so even this rule still lets a Master beat the vampire with a level 1 Spell, if HER level in the Sphere is high enough).<br /> <br /> We could, and actually should, remember that each game-line not only makes assumptions about the world, it assumes that other supernaturals are using the line's stats instead of its own stats. So Werewolf expect vampires to be using powers similar to Gifts and Spirit Charms, in Vampire werewolves have innate (and some not-so-innate) Disciplines and a Blood Pool (even if one that is filled by emotion instead of actual blood), and in Mage everyone uses static Rotes, that work like Magick nonetheless, with the advantage of being Paradox-Free and no disadvantage whatsoever. It isn't Dynamic, of course, so that means they're mostly stuck with their Rotes, and that's a world of advantage for Mages, but still follow the same rules.<br /> <br /> So, what that means? Aside what everyone already knows about how the rules aren't meant for crossovers, it does mean that those creatures ARE meant to have resources. They ARE meant in each setting to be able to deal with the &quot;natives'&quot; powers, simply because they mechanically draw on the same resources. In vampire, a Werewolf CAN be created with lower equivalent generation (to account for her Rank, maybe), and reap ALL the benefits of it, including powers of higher level. In Werewolf a vampire with access to a level 4 &quot;Gift&quot; is already an elder, or at least an Ancillae, and you can expect Methuselahs to have the equivalent of a Level 6 Gift, so Presence 7 isn't even a thing, indeed, simply because it isn't meant to exist. And if those things are silly from the POV of Mage and Werewolf, in the POV of Vampire it is ridiculous to think that a beginning character can beat the elders at their game.<br /> <br /> I don't want to discuss more here about what makes sense or not. This isn't the thread for that. I don't like the rule, either, but as I said, it is official and that is the only thing we can rely, if barely, given the rules of the thread itself. And its naive proposition.<br /> <br /> <b>Rahod</b>, I don't think neither that the Garou would hide, nor that it would help them. First because the other two groups, even not having the easy access to the Umbra, are far better than the werewolves in hiding. Second because they would have to come to the material to fight anyone who stands anyway, and that means that the actual fight still won't be in the Umbra. At this stage, it will probably be hard to use the Umbra for the assault, because any remaining forces will have the knowledge and resources to protect themselves. Mages have ways to deal with the Umbra and its denizens, even with Paradox and not entering there (which they can do and wipe the werewolves anyway, there are no Paradox in the Umbra), while Vampires already live in places usually of high Gauntlet, and after facing Mages, they are likely to learn something about how to block Umbral invasions (not to say about the ones with Spiritus and other Umbra-Related Disciplines).<br /> <br /> By the way, to really hide in the Umbra the werewolves would have to leave their Caerns unprotected, so they can expect to lose one of their most important assets, and maybe some power due to loss of face and Rank for letting ALL THEIR CAERNS FALL. In fact, it isn't an option at all.<br /> <br /> About vampires not having the supernatural power to deal with the others, I can only think you don't know Vampire at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:40:15-07:00","id":663163,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are the strongest at player-character levels. Mages are the strongest low NPC levels. The tip-top NPC are all basically omnipotent, so there's no real point in discussing them.<br /> Vampires get screwed in any war that doesn't involve the omnipotent NPCs. They are helpless 12 hours out of every 24, and are kind of meh even at night. They are low-mobility creatures fighting creatures who can teleport to another dimension to escape bad situations, or walk past defenses and appear on top of your head. Really vampires can't remotely compete with werewolves ability to teleport to the umbra, and mage's combo of correspondance and spirit. Their mobility and information disadvantage is absolutely crushing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T12:19:05-07:00","id":663333,"title":"","content":"Honestly I doubt we will ever come to a consensus on this. If we're talking about a battle royale with the factions being pretty much like they are in canon only united then I'd have to say mages, but if we start adding in Caine and entities that are pretty much gods then the end result isn't quite as certain.<br /> <br /> Apparently Lilith managed to kill Caine in one of the gehenna scenarios but I'm not really buying it. I think his immortality is probably more like that of Alucard from Hellsing, in that he can't die unless he wants to. I don't know where I read it but I believe it says in one of the core books that when it comes to Caine's power, whatever he wants to do he can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}